 "area": "field",
 "description": "SHARED DISSIPATIVE RELAXATION == MAP INFERENCE (block 197000). ONE integer dynamics, two frames differing only by a relabel. A field of FieldCell{val,obs,par} on 4-connected `adj` edges settles toward the minimum of E(x)=lam*\u03a3(x-obs)^2 + \u03a3_edges(x-x_j)^2 by RED-BLACK EXACT integer coordinate descent: the single `batch` rule df_relax updates only cells with par==phase, each to its conditional integer argmin cand=IDiv(2*(lam*obs+\u03a3nbr val)+den, 2*den), den=lam+deg. Non-adjacent same-colour cells make one half-sweep exact block coordinate descent, so the integer energy is monotone non-increasing to a fixed point (PHYSICS: 2nd-law dissipation; the free energy decreases, entropy is produced). RELABELED (val->MAP estimate, obs->noisy observation y, lam->likelihood precision, E->neg-log-posterior) the SAME run is MAP inference over a Gaussian MRF: the fixed point IS the MAP percept (COGNITION: denoising / filling-in). RelaxField.sign=-1 flips the SAME rule to reflected ascent (val<-2*val-cand), forcing E UP (anti-dissipative) -- and the percept recovery then diverges: break-one-breaks-both. OFF by default: fires only when a RelaxField{enabled=1} hub exists, which the measure adapter creates on opt-in; absent it, every existing path is byte-identical (FieldCell/RelaxField appear in no other graph). NO Rust, NO new Term.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "dissipation_inference",
  "description": "Dissipative relaxation of a field to the minimum of a quadratic energy IS MAP inference over a Gaussian MRF; the two are one integer computation read in two frames (the Gibbs distribution is the posterior; equilibrium is the MAP percept)."
 },
